      {
        "id": "ch02.s10.p04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch02.s10.p04.01",
            "text": "This is the central idea behind embeddings.",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s10.p04.02",
            "text": "Representing words as vectors can capture semantic meaning, allowing similar words to be grouped together and dissimilar words to be farther apart.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@729",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@732",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@736",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@738",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@742",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@745",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@747",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@750",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@753",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@755",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@758",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@778",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@780",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@782",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@784",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4092",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4097",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4100",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4102"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s10.p04.03",
            "text": "These vectors are called vector embeddings or token embeddings because each token is converted into a vector embedding.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@812",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@815",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@818",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@820",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@822",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@827"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s10.p04.04",
            "text": "Representing words as vectors so that semantic relationships are preserved is called vector embedding, and it is also called token embedding.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@973",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@975",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@977",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@980",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@982",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4127",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4130",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4132",
              "mk-6cFebjis@4134"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch02.s10.p04.05",
            "text": "If token embeddings are trained properly, those vectors can carry meaning.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@987",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@989",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@992",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@994",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@997",
              "ghCSGRgVB_o@3330",
